hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15642","Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Yala ibn Ata informed us, from Umarah ibn Hadid, from Sakhr al-Ghamidi, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, bless my nation in its early morning. He said: When he sent a detachment or an army, he sent them at the beginning of the day. He said: Sakhr was a merchant man, and he used to send his trade at the beginning of the day, so he became rich and his wealth increased."
"15643","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, he said: Yala ibn Ata informed me, he said: I heard Umarah ibn Hadid, a man from Bajilah, he said: I heard Sakhr al-Ghamidi, a man from Azd, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Allah, bless my nation in its early morning. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he sent a detachment, sent them at the beginning of the day. Sakhr was a merchant man, and he had slaves, and he used to send his slaves at the beginning of the day. He said: So his wealth increased until he did not know where to put it."
